here's something you're going to love or  hate the 2017 range rover evoque  convertible this is the soft top version  of the small luxury crossover SUV that  range rover debuted a few years ago it's  the first convertible SUV that range  rover has ever made and the company says  the first modern luxury convertible SUV  ever this will definitely be a  polarizing vehicle some people are going  to love it because it's quirky and weird  and it's an odd shape and some people  are going to hate it because it's quirky  and weird and it's an odd shape Land  Rover made it to tap into the growing  luxury SUV market and to piggyback on  the considerable success that the evoke  has had since its inception it looks  like the original evoke except for a few  minor aesthetic changes on the front and  the addition of alloy wheels LED fog  lamps and some cool tech features inside  it comes with a black fabric top that  deploys in about 18 seconds I like that  this convertible has considerable room  in the trunk more than most plus it has  to roll over protection bars that will  pop out at a milliseconds notice if you  happen to flip this thing the evoke  convertible has the same 240 horsepower  four-cylinder engine and 9-speed  automatic transmission as its hardtop  sister it comes with an active drive  that will switch between front and  all-wheel drive depending on road  conditions and we'll go to 60 miles per  hour in 7.8 seconds so it's not the  fastest SUV ever but it's fast enough  and if you're the type to want a beefy  open-top ride that sits high like an SUV  but feels luxurious enough inside to  cruise down Rodeo Drive this is the one  for you pricing will start around 52  thousand dollars
 

